     "turnId": "tn_rd7k2m9q4x1v",
     "type": "message.completed",
     "actor": null,
     "data": {
      "text": "Keyed on the hash, the cache hits on every run where the lockfile hasn’t changed. On the last 20 runs that would have saved about **4 minutes a build**.\n\n## The change\n\nOne line in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: the key moves from the file’s modification time to its content.\n\n```yaml\n- uses: actions/cache@v4\n  with:\n    path: ~/.npm\n    key: npm-${{ runner.os }}-${{ hashFiles('package-lock.json') }}\n    restore-keys: npm-${{ runner.os }}-\n```\n\n`restore-keys` lets a run whose lockfile did change start from the nearest older cache instead of from nothing.\n\n## What it saves\n\n| Step | Now | With the fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| Install | 4m 12s | 18s |\n| Build | 1m 40s | 1m 40s |\n| Test | 2m 05s | 2m 05s |\n| **Total** | **7m 57s** | **4m 03s** |\n\n## Still slow after this\n\n1. **Tests run serially.** Vitest is pinned to one thread in `vitest.config.ts`; four would take the step to about 40s.\n2. **The Docker layer cache is off.** Each run rebuilds the base image, which costs another minute on the deploy job.\n3. The `lint` job installs everything again instead of sharing the cache.\n\nI opened [#318](https://github.com/acme/app/pull/318) with the cache fix only. Want me to take the test threads next?"
     }
    },
